<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/17/eng@/~part_IV__cl_18> <https://schema.org/text> "Where an addressee receives an electronic message, the addressee is entitled to regard the electronic message as being what the originator intended to send, and to act on that presumption, unless the addressee knew or should have known, had he exercised reasonable care or used any agreed procedure, that the transmission resulted in any error in the electronic message as received. Each electronic message to be regarded separately"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/17/eng@> .
